/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ARGON dissolved in liquid AMMONIA -- full Krichevsky-Kasarnovsky form.
  ===================================================================
  The same rigorous formulation as the H2-NH3 and N2-NH3 records in the
  catalogue:
      y phi_V P  =  x gamma2* H(T) exp[ v_inf (P - Ps_NH3) / RT ].

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  With no Henry pair, argon falls onto the Raoult rung
  and its "vapour pressure" at 250 K comes from an Antoine extrapolation ABOVE
  its critical temperature (Tc = 150.86 K).  In the synthesis loop's separator
  that gave K_Ar = 1.7 against K_N2 = 124 -- argon ~70x more soluble in liquid
  ammonia than nitrogen -- and 88 % of the argon left dissolved in the product
  instead of accumulating in the loop.  The purge, which is the heart of this
  case, was left without physical meaning.

  SOURCE DATA: IUPAC-NIST Solubility Data Series Vol. 4 (Argon), H. L. Clever
  (ed.), 1980, pp. 314-318 -- critical evaluation by C. L. Young (July 1978),
  who classifies the four available sets as TENTATIVE:

    Kaminishi, G., Kogyo Kagaku Zasshi 68 (1965) 419 [Int. Chem. Eng. 5 (1965)
      749, English translation] -- x_Ar at 273.15 / 298.15 / 323.15 K, 50.8 to
      199.9 bar.  The anchor set: it covers exactly the loop pressure.
    Matous, J.; Sobr, J.; Novak, J. P., Coll. Czech. Chem. Comm. 35 (1970)
      3757 -- x_Ar at 243.15-303.15 K, 27.7 and 47.1 bar.  The ONLY set that
      reaches below 273 K, i.e. that covers the separator at 250 K.
    Michels, A.; Dumoulin, E.; Van Dijk, J. J. Th., Physica 27 (1961) 886 --
      x_Ar AND y_Ar at 298.48-373.75 K up to 825 bar.  HELD OUT of the fit and
      used as independent validation.

  A CORRECTION APPLIED TO THE MATOUS DATA -- declared, not silent.
  As printed in the compilation (SDS-4 p. 317) the Matous values are 10x larger
  than Kaminishi's at the single overlap point (273.15 K: x = 0.0533 at 47.1
  bar against 0.00561 at 50.8 bar), which contradicts the critical evaluation's
  own statement ("good agreement in the overlapping ranges of these three
  latter studies").  Divided by ten, the overlap point reproduces Kaminishi's
  KK line to -1.8 % and all seven temperatures fall within +-4 % of the van't
  Hoff line between 273 and 303 K.  Reading them as 10^1 x_Ar is therefore the
  only reading consistent with the evaluation and with the other data set, and
  it is the one adopted here.  TO BE CONFIRMED against the original Matous
  1970 paper -- until then, this pair carries that inference.

  FIT (KK line, ln(f_Ar/x_Ar) vs P-Ps; f_Ar = y_Ar phi_Ar P with phi_Ar from
  SRK; y_Ar from the ammonia vapour enhancement factor calibrated on the y_Ar
  MEASURED by Michels at 298.48 K).  Maximum KK-line residuals: 0.6 %, 0.5 %
  and 3.6 % on Kaminishi's three isotherms -- the KK line describes the data up
  to 200 bar within the declared experimental error (+-1 % in x).
      273.15 K -> H = 7.35e8 Pa,  v_inf = 24.7 cm3/mol
      298.15 K -> H = 5.08e8 Pa,  v_inf = 18.2 cm3/mol
      323.15 K -> H = 3.18e8 Pa,  v_inf = 25.1 cm3/mol
  van't Hoff over the TEN points (Kaminishi 273-323 K + Matous/10 243-303 K):
      dH_diss = +9495 J/mol,  H_ref(298.15 K) = 4.87e8 Pa,  rms(ln H) = 6 %.

  INDEPENDENT VALIDATION (held out of the fit): Michels 1961 at 298.48 K,
  25-305 bar, a different laboratory and method, with y_Ar measured ->
  H = 4.56e8 Pa, i.e. -6 % from the adopted value.

  CONSISTENCY WITH THE FAMILY:  v_inf = 23 cm3/mol against 23 (N2) and 24 (H2)
  in the same solvent; dH_diss > 0 as for both of them (these gases are MORE
  soluble in hot ammonia).  H_ref(Ar)/H_ref(N2) = 0.57 in ammonia against 0.46
  in water (the catalogue's Ar-water / N2-water records): argon is ~1.8x more
  soluble than nitrogen in liquid ammonia -- the same order, not 70x.

  PROMOTED to the standard catalogue 2026-09-08 on Vitor's decision, from the
  case it was curated in.  Reproduce the whole fit with
  tutorials/plant/greenAmmoniaIndustrialN2/curation/Ar-NH3/fit-Ar-NH3.py.

  TWO COPIES EXIST TODAY, and the reason is stated rather than left to be
  discovered: that case is SEALED (`sealed true;`), which FORBIDS the runtime
  every catalogue fallback, so it must carry the record inside its own
  constant/ tree -- and it carries this one as an AUTHORED file its
  propertyManifest does not yet claim, because the pair did not exist in the
  catalogue when the case was imported.  Until `bin/choupo-import` is re-run
  on that case, the manifest neither verifies nor forbids its copy and the two
  are kept in step BY HAND.  That re-import is the remedy, and it is named
  here rather than assumed done.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
solute      Ar;
solvent     NH3;

gasSpecies        Ar;
dissolvedSpecies  Ar;
convention        Sander-Hxp-v1;
model       vantHoff;
H_ref       4.87e8 Pa;            // infinite-dilution reference fugacity, 298.15 K
T_ref       298.15 K;
enthalpy    9495 J/mol;           // dH_diss > 0: more soluble hot
v_inf       2.3e-5;               // m^3/mol -- KK Poynting (22.7 cm3/mol fitted)
margulesA   0.0;                  // J/mol -- gamma2* (x_Ar < 3 % in the data; ~0.1 % in the loop)
Trange      ( 243  323 );   // data 243.15-323.15 K -- the 250 K separator is INSIDE
